===Noun===
{{en-noun|-}}

# {{lb|en|Islam}} [[almsgiving|Almsgiving]], one of the [[five pillars]] of [[Islam]], in the [[form#Noun|form]] of an [[annual#Adjective|annual]] [[tax#Noun|tax]] on certain [[type#Noun|types]] of [[property#Noun|property]] which is then [[use#Verb|used]] for [[charitable]] [[purpose#Noun|purposes]].
#* {{quote-book|en|author=w:Ibn Battuta|chapter=Syria|translator=[[w:H. A. R. Gibb|H[amilton] A[lexander] R[osskeen] Gibb]]|title=[[w:The Rihla|The Travels of Ibn Baṭṭūṭa A.D. 1325–1354{{nb...|Translated with Revisions and Notes from the Arabic Text Edited by C[harles] Defrémery and B[eniamino] R[affaello] Sanguinetti by H. A. R. Gibb}}]]|location=Cambridge, Cambridgeshire|publisher=[[w:Cambridge University Press|University Press]] for the {{w|Hakluyt Society}}|year=1958|volume=I|page=72|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/workss2v110hakl/page/72/mode/1up|oclc=1014788231|passage=Amongst these stations is the well-known place called Qaṭyā, which the people pronounce Qaṭya, where '''''zakāt''''' is collected from the merchants, their goods are examined, and their baggage most rigorously searched.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=[[w:E. L. Peters|Emrys L[loyd] Peters]]|chapter=Aspects of Rank and Status among Muslims in a Lebanese Village|editor=w:Julian Pitt-Rivers|title=Mediterranean Countrymen: Essays in Social Anthropology of the Mediterranean|location=Paris|publisher=[[w:De Gruyter|Mouton and Co.]]|year=1963|page=170|oclc=439177938|newversion=republished in|editor2=Louise E. Sweet|title2=Peoples and Cultures of the Middle East: An Anthropological Reader|volume2=II (Life in the Cities, Towns, and Countryside)|location2=Garden City, N.Y.|publisher2=Natural History Press for the {{w|American Museum of Natural History}}|year2=1970|page2=88|pageurl2=https://archive.org/details/peoplescultureso0002loui/page/88/mode/1up|isbn2=978-0-385-00378-0|passage=Services given by the Sayyids are supposed to be free, but they should receive the '''''Zikat''''', or one tenth of the fruits of the earth.}}

